    "updated_at": "2023-02-13T08:43:26Z",
    "body": "Thus far validity has aimed to match RFC 3986 and RFC 3987. (I would be open to allowing all non-ASCII equally (minus surrogates) as it's converted to ASCII anyway. That would also bring it more in line to how we deal with non-ASCII generally.)\r\n\r\nThis relates to #379 as well.\r\n\r\nI think your rationale is quite sound though and I would be open to making this change. But this would be the first intentional deviation from RFC 3986 validity I think. Would love to hear from others as well.",
